    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but I'm seeing a lot of pushback lately from some major groups and even some high-profile CEOs who say these programs can actually be counterproductive or even discriminatory. Is there any real evidence that the business benefits are a fact, or is that more of a theoretical idea that hasn't been proven in the real world?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While strong corporate backing is growing, the evidence supporting direct ROI remains nuanced and context-dependent. Some studies link diversity to better problem-solving and market understanding, suggesting real business benefits. However, critics rightly point out that focusing on mandates without cultural change can lead to resistance and performative compliance. The proof lies in sustained, authentic commitment rather than simple program existence.",
